  "body": "[Bogus comment state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#bogus-comment-state) is the only state that doesn't eventually report error on U+0000 NULLs or doesn't shadow it by other error (e.g. NULL in named character reference). Is there any historical reason for that? Quick search in W3C mail archive didn't give any relevant results. ",
